  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0 — BREAKING: the SDK is now boring. Business data that changes on a SaaS release cadence (pricing tables, model → provider inference, model-id normalisation, cost estimation) has been REMOVED from the SDK so a new model or a price change never requires a customer upgrade. Deleted: TokensBillTools (cost-estimation helpers with hardcoded price table), ProviderParser.ProviderFromModel, ProviderParser.NormalizeModelId, SdkCost (internal price table). Shape-based fallback for unknown hosts now tags provider = host and lets the backend classify. Pre-flight cost estimates on ReplayPlan.Estimate are now always null; the actual cost lands in the customer's dashboard after a run. Backend serves the AI host allowlist via /api/config so a new provider domain is picked up within one poll interval (120s default). What remained: HTTP interception, response body parsing for the four wire shapes (OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses, Anthropic, Google), host-based provider labelling, prompt hash, fire-and-forget queue. 0.9.2 — Non-streaming >32KB tail-tee; DiagnosticSubscriber emits prompt_hash; OpenAI stream finish_reason from prior chunk; /v1/responses recognised.",
